===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=disease|af|pneumono->lung|ultra->beyond|microscopic>tiny|silico->silicon|volcano>mountain|coniosis>dust inhaling disease|tree=1}}
Coined by Everett K Smith, President of the {{w|National Puzzlers' League}}, at their convention in 1935 as a deliberately long word. From {{af|en|pneumono-<t:lung>|ultra-<t:beyond>|microscopic|silico-|volcano|coniosis<t:dust>}}, as an extension of the medical term {{m|en|pneumonoconiosis}}.

